net: airoha: PPE bind failure diagnostics for AN7581 (201-06)

Runtime-instrumented airoha_eth / airoha_ppe to locate the broken
UNB -> BND promotion path on ZN504XG-D.  On the affected device the
driver *accepts* netfilter flowtable rules ([HW_OFFLOAD] entries
appear in conntrack), the hardware *learns* UNBIND entries
(/sys/kernel/debug/ppe/entries grows), yet /sys/kernel/debug/ppe/bind
stays at 0 forever, so all WAN traffic is CPU-forwarded.

The promotion chain is: PPE hits an UNBIND entry above the rate
threshold -> RX descriptor reports cpu_reason=0x0f
(PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED) -> airoha_ppe_check_skb()
(rate-limited per hash) -> airoha_ppe_foe_insert_entry() compares the
learned entry against the software pending table -> commit to SRAM
(BND).  This patch logs every gate in that chain, plus every reject
gate in airoha_ppe_flow_offload_replace(), at pr_info_ratelimited
with the "20106-ppe:" prefix.

Logging is on by default and can be toggled at runtime:
  echo 0 > /sys/module/airoha_eth/parameters/ppe_dbg_enabled

Verification on device:
  1. start a real TCP download (ICMP is never offloaded)
  2. dmesg | grep 20106
  3. wc -l /sys/kernel/debug/ppe/bind
Expected when healthy: "replace accepted", periodic
"check_skb: hash=...", "insert: committed sw->hw" and bind count > 0.

Generated against vanilla v6.18.52 + full huladabang/ponwrt@c3b518b
patch series.  Applies after 200-series ponwrt patches.  Diagnostic
only - no functional change besides the module parameter.
